From c8ce37462b2356528fba77c106c8c6fa5968abd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:25:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront tests: derivative of the flow rule of
 DigitSeparatorTest

The flow rule of the DigitSeparatorTest behaviour computed the flow rate
`f` but not its derivative `df_dseq` (MFront reports it by a warning). The
local Newton solver and the consistent tangent operator read this
uninitialized member, so that the results depended on the content of the
stack. The derivative is now computed.
---
 mfront/tests/behaviours/DigitSeparatorTest.mfront | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/mfront/tests/behaviours/DigitSeparatorTest.mfront b/mfront/tests/behaviours/DigitSeparatorTest.mfront
index 8a74d3444..137c375d4 100644
--- a/mfront/tests/behaviours/DigitSeparatorTest.mfront
+++ b/mfront/tests/behaviours/DigitSeparatorTest.mfront
@@ -11,4 +11,5 @@
 
 @FlowRule{
   f = de0 * pow(seq / s0, E);
+  df_dseq = de0 * E * pow(seq / s0, E - 1) / s0;
 }
\ No newline at end of file
